WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.840
The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) is a landmark
cancer genomics program to molecularly characterized

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:18.240
over 11,000 primary cancer and matched normal
samples spanning 33 cancer types.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.600
The joint effort between NCI and the National
Human Genome Research Institute began in 2006,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.769
bringing together researchers from diverse
disciplines and multiple institutions.

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:36.880
Over the past 15 years, TCGA has generated
over 2.5 petabytes of genomic, epigenomic,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.550
transcriptomic, and proteomic data.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:45.010
The data, which has already led to improvements
in our ability to diagnose, treat, and prevent

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:50.399
cancer, will remain publicly available for
anyone in the research community to use.

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:55.750
All data collected and processed by the program
is currently available at the NCI Cancer Research

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.800
Data Commons (CRDC).

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.650
The NCI Cancer Research Data Commons (CRDC)
is a cloud-based data science infrastructure

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:08.360
that connects data sets with analytics tools
to allow users to share, integrate, analyze,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.830
and visualize cancer research data to drive
scientific discovery.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:19.630
In addition to the TCGA data, CRDC also provides
access to data from other NCI programs such

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:24.170
as the Therapeutically Applicable Research
to Generate Effective Treatments (TARGET),

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:32.420
and The Clinical Proteomics Tumor Analysis
Consortium (CPTAC), through various platforms:

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.610
• Genomic Data Commons (GDC)
• Proteomic Data Commons (PDC)

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:42.030
• Imaging Data Commons (IDC)
• Cancer Data Service (CDS)

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:48.660
• Integrated Canine Data Commons (ICDC)
• Clinical Trial Data Commons (CTDC)

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:54.500
The Genomic Data Commons (GDC) Data Portal
provides users with web-based access to data

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.250
from cancer genomics studies.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.390
The front page displays a summary of all available
datasets.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:06.500
The GDC Data Portal provides five navigation
options for browsing available harmonized

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.330
datasets.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:14.160
These include the navigations based on project,
exploration, analysis, repository or human

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.500
anatomical sites.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:22.110
Each view provides a distinct representation
of the same underlying set of GDC data and

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.110
metadata.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:28.460
The toolbar available at the top of all pages
in the GDC Data Portal also provides convenient

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.850
navigation links and access to authentication
and quick search.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:38.230
The left portion of this toolbar provides
access to the Home Page, Projects Page, Exploration

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:42.840
Page, Analysis Page, and a link to Repository
Page.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.100
The right portion of this toolbar provides
access to quick search, manage sets, authentication

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.180
functions, the cart, and the GDC Apps menu.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:58.200
The Projects link directs users to the Projects
Page, which gives an overall summary of project-level

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.540
information, including the available data
for each project.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.660
It also provides filtering, navigation, and
advanced visualization features that allow

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.800
users to identify and browse projects of interest.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:16.860
On the left, a panel of facets allow users
to apply filters to find projects of interest.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:21.250
When facet filters are applied, the table
and visualizations on the right are updated

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.310
to display only the matching projects.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:28.240
When no filters are applied, all projects
are displayed.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.170
The top right side of the Projects Page displays
a few visualizations of the data such as the

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:38.550
Top Mutated Genes in Selected Projects and
Case Distribution per Project.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:42.959
Hovering the cursor over each bar will display
information about the number of cases affected

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:47.250
by the disease type and clicking on each bar
will launch the Gene Summary Page for the

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.430
gene associated with the mutation.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:55.040
Users can toggle the Y-Axis of this bar graph
between a percentage or raw number of cases

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.040
affected.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:01.460
Below these graphs is a table that contains
a list of projects and details about each

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:05.180
project, such as the number of cases and data
files.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:10.720
The table provides links to Project Summary
Pages in the Project ID column.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.180
Columns with file and case counts include
links to open the corresponding files or cases

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.509
in Repository Page.

00:04:17.509 --> 00:04:22.180
The Graph tab contains an interactive view
of information in the Table tab.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:27.490
The numerical values in Case Count, File Count,
and File Size columns are represented by bars

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.500
of varying length according to size.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.300
These columns are sorted independently in
descending order.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:39.210
Mousing over an element of the graph connects
it to associated elements in other columns,

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:43.210
including Project ID and major Primary Sites.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:47.950
Most elements in the graph are clickable,
allowing the user to open the associated cases

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.080
or files in Repository Page.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.840
Like the projects table, the graph will reflect
any applied facet filters.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:01.760
The Exploration Page allows users to explore
data in the GDC using advanced filters, which

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:05.520
includes those on a gene and mutation level.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:10.340
Users choose filters on specific Cases, Genes
or Mutations on the left of this page and

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.660
then can visualize these results on the right.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:18.940
There is also a Clinical tab with filters
that apply specifically to clinical data.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:24.120
As users add filters to the data on the Exploration
Page, the Results section will automatically

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.260
be updated.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:31.950
Results are divided into different tabs: Cases,
Genes, Mutations, and OncoGrid.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:37.360
The Cases tab gives an overview of all the
cases who correspond to the filters chosen.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:41.810
The top of this section contains a few pie
graphs with categorical information regarding

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:47.130
the Primary Site, Project, Disease Type, Gender,
and Vital Status.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:52.220
Below these pie charts is a tabular view of
cases, which can be exported, sorted and saved

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.630
using the buttons on the right.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:06:00.030
The Case Summary Page displays case details
including the project and disease information,

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:05.260
data files that are available for that case,
and the experimental strategies employed.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:10.919
The Genes tab will give an overview of all
the genes that match the criteria of the filters.

00:06:10.919 --> 00:06:16.080
The top of this tab contains a bar graph of
the most frequently mutated genes.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.170
Hovering over each bar in the plot will display
information about the percentage of cases

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:21.790
affected.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:25.540
In addition, this section contains a survival
curve.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:30.169
The survival curve is calculated using the
Kaplan-Meier estimator based on all cases

00:06:30.169 --> 00:06:35.070
with survival data within the specified Exploration
Page search.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:40.510
Users may choose to download the underlying
data in JSON or TSV format or an image of

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:47.350
the graph in SVG or PNG format by clicking
the download icon at the top of each graph.

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:52.180
Gene Summary Pages describe each gene with
mutation data and provides results related

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.570
to the analyses that are performed on these
genes.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:07:00.630
A table shows how many cases are affected
by mutations and copy number variation within

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.820
the gene as a ratio and percentage.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:08.540
Under the protein view, mutations and their
frequency across cases are mapped to a graphical

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.259
visualization of protein-coding regions with
a lollipop plot.

00:07:12.259 --> 00:07:18.300
Pfam domains are highlighted along the x-axis
to assign functionality to specific protein-coding

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.800
regions.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:24.050
The bottom track represents a view of the
full gene length.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:28.860
Different transcripts can be selected by using
the drop-down menu above the plot.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:33.330
The panel to the right of the plot allows
the plot to be filtered by mutation consequences

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:34.860
or impact.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:39.410
The plot will dynamically change as filters
are applied.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:43.820
Mutation consequence and impact is denoted
in the plot by color.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:48.580
The Mutations tab contains information about
one somatic mutation and how it affects the

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:50.520
associated gene.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:56.490
Each mutation is identified by its chromosomal
position and nucleotide-level change.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.759
A table shows how many cases are affected
by the particular mutation.

00:08:00.759 --> 00:08:05.780
You can compare the effects of different mutations
on the survival curve.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:10.810
The Exploration Page also includes an OncoGrid
plot of the cases with the most mutations,

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:16.080
for the top 50 mutated genes affected by high
impact mutations.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:21.320
Genes displayed on the left of the y-axis
correspond to individual cases on the X-axis.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:26.720
Additionally, the plot also indicates in each
cell any CNV events detected for these top

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:29.400
mutated cases and genes.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:33.500
The grid is color-coded with a legend at the
top which describes what type of mutation

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:39.519
consequence and CNV event is observed for
each gene and case combination.

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:43.329
Clinical information and the available data
for each case are available at the bottom

00:08:43.329 --> 00:08:45.129
of the grid.

00:08:45.129 --> 00:08:50.230
In addition to the Exploration Page, the GDC
Data Portal also has features used to save

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:54.029
and compare sets of cases, genes, and mutations.

00:08:54.029 --> 00:08:59.809
These sets can either be generated with existing
filters or through custom selection.

00:08:59.809 --> 00:09:02.410
There are three tabs on this page.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:09.119
The users can select either to do Set Operations,
Cohort Comparison or Clinical Data Analysis.

00:09:09.119 --> 00:09:14.490
The Results tab is where users can view the
results of current or previous set analyses.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:21.879
Finally, the Repository Page is the primary
method of accessing data in the GDC Data Portal.

00:09:21.879 --> 00:09:27.259
The individual file can either be downloaded
individually from File Summary Pages or collected

00:09:27.259 --> 00:09:30.910
in the file cart to be downloaded as a bundle.

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:35.279
Clicking on the shopping cart icon that is
next to any item in the GDC will add the item

00:09:35.279 --> 00:09:36.069
to your cart.

